.page native 1 run a program under the native system call personality

# SYNOPSIS
*native* _PROGRAM_ [_ARGUMENT_...]

# DESCRIPTION
`native` starts _PROGRAM_ (searched for through `PATH`) as a native TouhouOS program. Every process normally is one; the command exists for the opposite case: a program started with `linux(1)` keeps the Linux personality across `execve`, so it cannot start a native tool with a plain exec. `native` selects the native personality for the next exec and runs the program.

# EXIT STATUS
The exit status of the program. 2 for a missing operand, 126 if the program could not be run, 127 if it was not found.

# EXAMPLES
    native ls /

# SEE ALSO
linux(1)
